%U A399036 2788231034537754185847018535,49343325808367627766067771877552,1746530369619461203855177355250362701
%N A399036 Number of unlabeled reducible flow graphs with n nodes whose entry is a global source (in-degree 0, reaches every node), self-loops disallowed.
%C A399036 The global source is unique, so plain isomorphism suffices.
%C A399036 The self-loops-allowed version equals the unlabeled reducible distinguished-entry count (loop-encoding bijection preserves reducibility).
%C A399036 Computed exactly by the equivariant Burnside recurrence (see _reducible_unlabeled in the linked program of A397968).
%D A399036 F. Harary and E. M. Palmer, Graphical Enumeration, Academic Press, NY, 1973.
%D A399036 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Flow graph reducibility, SIAM J. Comput. 1 (1972), 188-202.
%D A399036 M. S. Hecht and J. D. Ullman, Characterizations of reducible flow graphs, J. ACM 21 (1974), 367-375.
%D A399036 R. W. Robinson, Counting digraphs with restrictions on the strong components, in T.-H. Ku (ed.), Combinatorics and Graph Theory '95, World Scientific, Singapore, 1995, pp. 343-354.
%D A399036 R. E. Tarjan, Testing flow graph reducibility, J. Comput. System Sci. 9 (1974), 355-365.
%F A399036 a(n) = (1/(n-1)!) * Sum over cycle types mu of n-1 elements of permcount(mu) * F_S(mu), where F_S is the equivariant SCC-region recurrence specialized to a fixed global source.
%o A399036 (Python) unlabeled_reducible_sequence("unlabeled_reducible_single_source", 16) # See Python link in A397968 for program code.
%Y A399036 Cf. A397968 (equivalent loopy single-source version), A350360 (all single-source digraphs).
%K A399036 nonn,new
%O A399036 1,3
%A A399036 _Gregory Morse_, Sep 14 2026
